From e7f21991126ae48c24ba8d77f78cbb920500d9b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lionel Debieve <lionel.debieve@foss.st.com>
Date: Sun, 3 May 2026 14:38:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 778/913] drivers: stm32_risaf: fix warning when building for
 aarch32
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

STM32MP2 can execute a secure OS compiled for aarch32.
When compiling the RISAF driver a warning occurs :
core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risaf.c:529:30: error:
format ‘%lx’ expects argument of type ‘long unsigned int’,
but argument 6 has type ‘paddr_t’ {aka ‘long long unsigned int’}
[-Werror=format=]
  529 | EMSG("RISAF %#"PRIxPTR": unsupported encryption mode",
      |      ^~~~~~~~~~
  530 |      risaf->pdata.base.pa);
      |      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
      |                       |
      |                       paddr_t {aka long long unsigned int}

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git e633db7dd5804f05e6ab18f36ee7576f67a8094d drivers: stm32_risaf: fix warning when building for aarch32]
Signed-off-by: Lionel Debieve <lionel.debieve@foss.st.com>
Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Change-Id: Iecdc63d6b9ca50f3f7b6e8a68c2b0baa74072670
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/optee/optee_os/+/571875
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risaf.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risaf.c b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risaf.c
index f52da5273..5b6ec4dc8 100644
--- a/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risaf.c
+++ b/core/drivers/firewall/stm32_risaf.c
@@ -526,7 +526,7 @@ risaf_configure_region(struct stm32_risaf_instance *risaf,
 		 * for another platform.
 		 */
 		if (!IS_ENABLED(CFG_STM32MP21) && (cfg & BIT(14))) {
-			EMSG("RISAF %#"PRIxPTR": unsupported encryption mode",
+			EMSG("RISAF %#"PRIxPA": unsupported encryption mode",
 			     risaf->pdata.base.pa);
 			return TEE_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED;
 		}
-- 
2.53.0

